{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read-only doc preflight. Do not edit anything. Do not delegate further.\n\nRead GitHub issue #11 (`gh issue view 11`) and spec #4 (`gh issue view 4`, plus its comments for the probe findings), then the existing code it builds on: src/status_record.rs, src/runner.rs, src/job_registry.rs, src/stream.rs, src/finalize.rs, src/prompt.rs, src/models.rs, src/capability.rs, tests/e2e.rs, Cargo.toml.\n\nList, max 250 words total, one line each:\n1. Contradictions between #11, #4 and the existing code.\n2. Defaults or formats nothing states but the lane must pick (job id format, status-record path and JSON shape, heartbeat interval, watch output format, watch exit code on timeout, where the binary target lives).\n3. Failure cases with no stated behaviour or error output.\n4. Acceptance criteria that fight the spec or the code.\nFor each, give your recommended ruling in a few words. End with STATUS line.\n\nContext: #7 (the tracer, in progress) adds a detached supervisor and the CLI with these owner rulings: `gh issue view 7 --comments`. Assume #7 lands as ruled; flag where #11 conflicts with those rulings. Skip question 2's #7-specific examples; list #11's own unstated defaults.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"a592e948-93da-4c3d-a67c-1f8d125d3b0d"}
